## Independent Pixel Inventory

The source has one vertical column of six **separate** horizontal number-line
subfigures. Each has one blunt left end, one right arrow, three distinct
collinear point markers, and three matching coordinate labels below the line.
Subfigure letters are to the left. There are six lines, six arrows, six subfigure
labels, and 18 point/label pairs. No numerical scale, origin, unit marks, ticks,
vertical axis, or function curve appears.

| English row | Source letter | Source baseline y | Left-to-right point/label pairs and approximate source x | Adjacent positive drawing displacements |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| a) | U+0430 | 31 | A(x):266, B(x squared):352, C(x cubed):471 | A->B 58.48; B->C 80.92 |
| b) | U+0431 | 123 | C(x cubed):209, A(x):357, B(x squared):651 | C->A 100.64; A->B 199.92 |
| c) | U+0432 | 216 | C(x cubed):211, B(x squared):416, A(x):506 | C->B 139.40; B->A 61.20 |
| d) | U+0433 | 306 | A(x):269, C(x cubed):476, B(x squared):714 | A->C 140.76; C->B 161.84 |
| e) | U+0434 | 397 | B(x squared):239, C(x cubed):476, A(x):740 | B->C 161.16; C->A 179.52 |
| f) | U+0435 | 489 | B(x squared):242, A(x):448, C(x cubed):740 | B->A 140.08; A->C 198.56 |

Source line ends are approximately x=90 and x=887. The same horizontal
factor 0.68 is applied to every point and line endpoint. Canvas baselines
are regularized to screen y=30,94,158,222,286,350. These are drawing
coordinates, not selected values of x or exact numerical distances.
Visible coordinate labels typeset the exponents as superscripts.

For each row the inventory maps its three point IDs plus its own arrow and
subfigure-label object. `requires: ["pointRelationships"]` is present on all
six groups. Every point is covered by the wholly intra-group three-point
collinearity assertion and adjacent ordered-displacement assertions.
Each point additionally has its own line-membership assertion; each arrow has
a connects assertion. Total: 42 assertions, including 12 ordered displacements,
6 collinearities, 18 own-line memberships, and 6 arrow connections. No
`objectCount` assertion is used.

## Fidelity Doubts and Regularization

- Visual point-center/arrow-tip estimates are approximate to about +/-2 source
  pixels. The task itself describes approximate positions, not a measured scale.
- Uneven raster ink and tiny white pinholes, especially row e's middle and
  right markers, do not have an open-point legend. Uniform filled markers are
  a disclosed modern regularization requiring the independent reviewer's
  judgment, not an asserted extra source fact.
- Source ordering, distinctness, label ownership, six independent lines, and
  right arrow directions are clear. Row spacing, stroke noise, font, and
  marker consistency were regularized openly.
- No possible/impossible verdict, origin, -1/+1 marker, solution, or choice
  was drawn. No function curve was substituted for the number lines.

